Gemini:
The wind beats, howling down from the mountains through the ravines;
A woman stands on a cliff, gazing at the river, her hair unbound;
She reminds me of a star whose light has faded, with pale, trembling lips.
She utters no sound… startled, she shudders as she looks down at the river;
How dreadfully it roars, how dreadfully it flows!
The snarling, cruel black valley rages;
If only someone would urge her: "Do not kill yourself!"
The woman closed her eyes and swiftly plunged into the whirlpool.

